# Session log — {slug}

> Ephemeral, gitignored. LIVE state of THIS change, re-read after any compaction (LAW5).
> Ordered by reading urgency: what blocks / what's next is at the TOP (read first).
> A line earns its place only if it is LIVE. The moment something stops being live
> (a chunk closes, a decision is superseded, a render is approved) it LEAVES this file:
> durable outcome -> graduate to decisions.md / proposal / area doc; scaffolding -> delete.
> This is NOT a history log. Size is a consequence, never a target.
>
> Sections, in read order:
>   1. AWAITING OWNER — blocking gates: what needs the owner's approval before done/commit
>   2. NOW            — the one open chunk / immediate next step
>   3. Live decisions — decisions currently in force (superseded ones have left)
>   4. Discarded      — approaches rejected in this front, one line each (don't retry)
>   5. Goal           — 1-2 lines pointing at proposal.md (context, not action)
>   6. Chunks         — index only: [x] done / [ ] pending, no narrative
>   7. Files in scope — paths this change touches and their role

